.TH "GLESHA-UPLOAD" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-upload \- upload a file to remote buckets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha upload\fR FILE \-\-to REMOTE... [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Upload FILE to every remote named by \-\-to, in parallel. No backup set is involved. An existing object is only replaced with \-\-force.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-key KEY
Object key (default: the file name).
.TP
.B \-\-force
Replace an existing object.
.TP
.B \-\-storage\-class CLASS
AWS storage class (default: STANDARD). Classes other than STANDARD require an AWS remote.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Upload to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory, or 128MiB). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. On Linux, the default is half of the available memory. On other systems, or if the available memory cannot be read, the default is 128MiB.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Run up to N transfers at once (default: 4). The memory limit may lower the effective number.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Hash up to N files at once (default: 4).
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha upload documents.tar.xz.gpg \-\-to b2
glesha upload documents.tar.xz.gpg \-\-to aws,b2 \-\-key backups/documents.gpg
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-check (1),
.BR glesha\-download (1)
